-- DH-Tools: Modules\DHBavin\ItemPoints.lua
-- Static reference data only - no logic. Maps item NAME (not itemID) to
-- the "Bavin Points" value Loopi's guild uses to price donations, for
-- Tooltip.lua's OnTooltipSetItem hook to display.
--
-- WHY NAME, NOT ITEMID: this table is keyed by exact item display name on
-- purpose. WoW's "of the X" random-suffix rare items (Ranger Boots of the
-- Owl, Ranger Boots of the Tiger, etc.) all share ONE base itemID - the
-- suffix is a random enchantment applied at drop time, not a separate
-- item entry - but the source spreadsheet prices each suffix differently.
-- An itemID-keyed table cannot represent that; a name-keyed one can.
--
-- itemId IS still included per entry as supplementary metadata - NOT used
-- as the lookup key, and deliberately allowed to repeat across multiple
-- suffix-variant names that share one base item. nil where no confident
-- single itemID match could be established.
--
-- SOURCE: Loopi's "DH Reputation.xlsx" (Items sheet, columns A/G/P),
-- matched by name against the nexus-devs/wow-classic-items community item
-- database (exact match, then "of the X" suffix base-name stripping, then
-- a Potion/Elixir naming swap for Classic-Era-vs-that-DB differences, then
-- a short hand-verified list of typo/plural/apostrophe fixes). Both 0 and
-- negative point values are intentional (Loopi confirmed 2026-08-04).
-- A sheet row name that appears more than once (two conflicting point
-- values under the same exact name) is resolved automatically: keep the
-- HIGHER-points row, points and detail together from that same row (never
-- mixed across rows) - see _build-itempoints.ps1 and claude\knowledge\k-0052.
--
-- detail (added 2026-08-06) = column P's plain-text summary line verbatim
-- ("<name>: <points> pts to Bavin; <price/source>"), nil where the sheet
-- row had no column P value. Tooltip.lua's USE_DETAIL_LINE toggle picks
-- whether to show this or the plain points number - see that file.
--
-- goldValue (added 2026-09-28, DH-Store question #5) = the sheet's own
-- PurchaseVal column, the precise per-unit gold price as a plain decimal
-- (e.g. 50.34 = 50g 34s) - NOT the rounded "Val" column, NOT copper. nil
-- where the sheet had no gold price for this item (points-only donation
-- rows). DH-Store\Core.lua reads this via DHTools.Bavin.GetItemGoldValue -
-- this table itself has no logic, same as every other field here.
--
-- Generated by claude\DH-Bavin\intake\_build-itempoints.ps1 (2026-08-04,
-- detail field added 2026-08-06, goldValue field added 2026-09-28).
-- MAINTENANCE: not synced or editable in-game - at ~7000 entries this is
-- far too large for the guild addon-message sync channel. To update, give
-- Loopi a refreshed spreadsheet, re-run the build script, ship next release.

local DHTools = DHTools
DHTools.Bavin = DHTools.Bavin or {}
local ns = DHTools.Bavin

